WEBVTT

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.130
Zero kara kakedashite

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.130
Start running from the beginning,

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.500
Omoi dake wo dakishimete

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.500
with nothing but your emotions in your hands.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.890
Sonomama kakenukete

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.890
Just keep running...

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:18.350
Itsumo koko de mitsumeteru

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:18.350
I'm always watching you from here.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:42.300
Hajimete deatta hi no manazashi wasurenai

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:42.300
I still remember your expression the day we first met.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:49.190
Taiyou mitai ni kokoro wo terashitekureta

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:49.190
It lit up my heart like the sun.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:56.960
Asu no yukue sagashite nayandeiru nara

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:56.960
If you're anxious about where to go tomorrow,

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:06.890
Ima kimi no tame ni akari ni naritai yo

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:06.890
I want to become a beacon to you.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.010
Zero kara tobidatte

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.010
Start flying from the beginning.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.380
Ima no kimi wo toki hanachi

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.380
Let go of your current self...

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.730
Mugen ni habataite

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.730
and fly towards infinity.

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.600
Donna toki mo mimaru yo

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.600
I will always watch over you...

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.510
Kitto zutto tooku made

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.510
no matter how far you fly.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:36.080
Episode 32 - A Midsummer Night's Dream

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:38.500
Miss Ayumi, over here!

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:40.180
How does it feel to be the youngest ever winner...

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:41.980
of this prestigious prize?

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:44.490
She's as radiant as a queen!

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:48.360
There's no two ways about it: this girl was born to be a star.

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:53.660
It's Maya Kitajima... the girl who's in exile from the world of acting!

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:55.100
What's she doing here?

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:00.610
Maya, you made it.

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:03.710
I'm the one who asked Maya Kitajima to come.

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:07.160
I wanted to announce my successor for role of the Scarlet Angel.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:11.320
I think I've finally decided who I'd like to succeed me as the Scarlet Angel.

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:16.100
It will be Ayumi Himekawa.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.450
Ms. Tsukikage!

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:22.970
However, I'd also like to make another announcement.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:26.480
I would like to give Maya Kitajima one final chance.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:31.260
If she receives this award, or the equivalent Best Actress Award...

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:36.890
from the Japanese Acting Federation, within the next two years,

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:41.950
I'll reconsider my decision over who will play the Scarlet Angel.

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:45.530
If anything should happen to me during that time,

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:49.750
or if Maya Kitajima forfeits,

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:53.330
she will lose the chance to compete for the role,

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:56.380
and it and all associated rights will default to Ayumi Himekawa.

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:58.320
Ms. Tsukikage.

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:01.350
Is this what you meant when you said she had to improve drastically?

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:02.830
This is crazy...

00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:05.980
There isn't a single company that would accept Maya at the moment.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:09.190
Let's go home, Maya.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:13.670
Wait.

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:17.180
Ayumi!

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:19.530
You've got two years.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:21.970
I'll wait for two years.

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:25.990
And you better get this straight: I won't forgive you...

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:28.040
if you give up before then.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:30.230
If you try to forfeit or whatever,

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:34.010
I shall mock you for the rest of my life.

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:35.350
Do you understand?

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:36.380
You have two years.

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:40.060
I want to fight you for the role of the Scarlet Angel.

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:45.920
Ayumi, why would you say that to her?

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:49.260
Because I've never even beaten her once.

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:55.260
Yet, she's made me taste the bitterness of defeat on three separate occasions.

00:03:56.390 --> 00:03:58.140
How can I possibly win the Best Actress Award...

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:01.180
from the Acting Federation in the next two years?

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:07.210
It's beyond me...  the Scarlet Angel is beyond me!

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:13.080
Graduation

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:24.470
I'll never be able to perform in a play here again.

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:29.460
Where can I go to act now?

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:31.460
Maya,

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:34.830
come outside and come see this!

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:39.750
Hey, Maya!

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:41.310
Hi!

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:42.040
Guys...

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:44.150
Everyone came out to see you off.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:47.300
They wanted to give this school's one and only famous actress a good send-off!

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:50.020
Thanks, everyone!

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:54.520
I never would have imagined I'd get such a warm goodbye...

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:57.210
I'm so happy I took up acting!

00:04:57.910 --> 00:05:02.450
One Star Academy

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:04.530
Mr. Hijiri!

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:09.940
Mr. Purple Roses wanted to congratulate you on your graduation.

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:14.720
Would you please give this to him for me?

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:20.480
It was thanks to him that I even got the chance to come to this fantastic school.

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:23.910
Please tell him: "Thank you for three great years!"

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:26.520
Why?

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:29.130
Why would she give me something so valuable?

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:29.980
You have to take it back to her!

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:35.020
No, she wanted you to have it precisely because it's so important to her.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:38.350
You'd only upset her if you tried to give it back.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:45.540
What kind of girl just gives someone like me her yearbook and diploma?

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:47.810
Congratulations!

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:50.600
You've finally made it and now, you can enter university.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:53.800
You've passed grade, middle and high school - all at the top of your class.

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:57.560
Your grades were very impressive, considering how heavily involved you were in show business!

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:00.390
I guess I'm just a geek.

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:04.200
You can't be serious!

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:10.850
It's a shame I couldn't make it to my graduation ceremony or the school trip.

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:13.610
I wouldn't have expected someone like you to care about such things.

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:14.210
Hmm?

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:17.070
Oh nothing... Just that you've always been a little different.

00:06:17.070 --> 00:06:19.730
You gave me the impression that you were someone special.

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:24.210
Someone special?

00:06:27.710 --> 00:06:31.080
I'm sorry I can't be around more, but I've got lots to work on.

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:35.520
If you get lonely and start missing me, you can pretend this is me singing you a lullaby!

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:41.260
My parents' entourage were always showering me with praise.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:45.810
I was spoiled and then, I started to believe the hype.

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:51.330
When I was five years old, I entered a beauty contest organized by a clothing designer,

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:55.410
and I was sure I would win.

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:59.930
But there was a girl there who was just so stunning that she stood out over all the rest.

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:03.860
Anyone could plainly see that she was the most beautiful girl there and yet somehow,

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:06.540
I was awarded first place and she only got second.

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:11.310
They said it would be better publicity if Mitsugu and Utako Himekawa's daughter...

00:07:11.310 --> 00:07:13.620
grabbed first prize.

00:07:16.390 --> 00:07:18.840
My, my, what's wrong?

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:23.670
Nursie, tell me the truth...

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:26.450
Do you really think I'm pretty?

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:28.820
What a silly question!

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:29.860
Don't laugh at me!

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:34.880
The people who come here always say that I'm pretty, but they're only saying that...

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:39.330
because of Mommy and Daddy, aren't they?

00:07:40.670 --> 00:07:42.990
You really are a beautiful little girl, Ayumi.

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:45.340
Look at your reflection in the mirror!

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:49.300
You're so pretty that even the fish are taken with you!

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:50.450
Nursie...

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:56.770
When you grow up, you'll be even more beautiful than your mother.

00:07:58.600 --> 00:07:59.840
Nursie!

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:10.130
Yes. Utako has rehearsals in the afternoon, so I'm sure she'll be there shortly.

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:15.100
Just wait for me, Alexander. We can play when I get home.

00:08:16.070 --> 00:08:18.880
I'll buy some cake before I come, Nursie.

00:08:18.880 --> 00:08:20.720
Can you please prepare the tea?

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:23.030
Yes, Queen Mary would be great.

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:27.060
And then, I have a favor to ask you when you wake up my mother.

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:34.550
They put up Ayumi Himekawa's picture again!

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:38.380
Yeah, and the teacher always pays more attention to her than anyone else!

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:40.460
She always gets special treatment.

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:43.180
It must be nice having famous parents.

00:08:43.720 --> 00:08:48.690
I was never given credit for having done anything off my own back.

00:08:49.390 --> 00:08:55.430
On Sports Day, my relay team was in last place...

00:08:55.770 --> 00:08:58.400
and I was the final runner.

00:08:58.400 --> 00:08:59.730
I refused to lose.

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:01.730
I simply did not want to lose.

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:02.910
There was only one runner ahead of me.

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:06.930
I would run!

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:09.650
I would run! I wouldn't falter!

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:12.960
My own strength!

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:16.100
Yes! I was feeling my own strength flowing through my body!

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:17.570
Give me more!

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:19.140
Give me more strength!

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:24.440
It was the first time my individual efforts had ever been acknowledged.

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:27.380
From then on, I'd like to be recognized....

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:29.600
for my own successes, not as my parents' child!

00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:34.170
Every day, I was confronted with competitors and put downs.

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:37.160
That's why I decided to give my all.

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:39.840
I knew that, using my own willpower, I could achieve anything.

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:42.680
That's right, my own willpower...

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:44.780
Give me more of my own willpower!

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:56.710
I found that acting opened up a world ruled by skill and everyone acknowledged my theatrical skills.

00:09:57.230 --> 00:09:58.790
I fell in love with the stage.

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:05.700
I've wanted to play the Scarlet Angel for years now.

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:07.860
What's the Scarlet Angel, Mother?

00:10:08.190 --> 00:10:12.580
The actress who plays is widely regarded as the very best actress in the whole of Japan.

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:14.890
It is a great honor.

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:18.690
It was at that point I decided that playing the Scarlet Angel would...

00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:23.800
mean people stop saying I'd only made it on the back of my parents.

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:27.670
If I was able to do that, I would finally step out from the shadows...

00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:30.310
of my parents' names.

00:10:33.430 --> 00:10:35.470
Thanks for bringing this, Ayumi.

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:36.720
I'm off home now.

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:38.520
Don't work too hard, Mom.

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:40.330
Ayumi...

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:43.100
Thanks for your wonderful wake-up call this morning.

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:50.540
I'm now aiming to clinch the role my mother wants so badly.

00:10:51.890 --> 00:10:55.430
I've given my all - in my studies or my rehearsals alike.

00:10:55.890 --> 00:11:00.000
Nobody can ever know about my blisters or my bleeding feet.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:03.800
People might perceive me as a genius, but it's only because I've battled for what I've achieved.

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:07.020
The real genius is Maya Kitajima.

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:11.300
That's why I want to fight her for the role of the Scarlet Angel.

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:14.390
If I don't, it'll all be meaningless.

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:19.190
Don't forget: I'll be waiting for you for the next two years.

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:20.130
Maya!

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:23.060
Ayumi?

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:33.500
Frankenstein's First Love

00:11:28.570 --> 00:11:31.590
Let's toast our show's success!

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:33.520
Cheers!

00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:39.550
The show was a real hit. We sold out every day for two weeks.

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:43.030
It's because you were the perfect Frankenstein!

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:44.520
Hey!

00:11:45.230 --> 00:11:48.870
I want to act with everyone.

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:53.450
I have two years to get the role of the Scarlet Angel and I'm not going to give up!

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:56.450
How can I give up before I've even begun to fight?

00:11:57.650 --> 00:12:00.630
Now, I know I said this show was a success and we sold out every night.

00:12:00.630 --> 00:12:06.050
However, this is a small theater and our audience is made up entirely of hardcore fans.

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:09.640
Fans are more lenient when it comes to overlooking mistakes,

00:12:09.640 --> 00:12:12.360
so we shouldn't just be content with what we managed here!

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:13.980
What we've achieved so far is just the starting point.

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:16.920
I want us to aim higher!

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:19.100
Don't you all want to perform in a bigger venue?

00:12:27.610 --> 00:12:31.480
I don't want to bankrupt myself by putting on a show by an unknown troupe.

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:35.480
Our venue only puts on plays with well-known actors or prestigious troupes.

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:39.470
No matter how good you are at acting, if you can't draw a crowd, it's not worth it.

00:12:39.470 --> 00:12:41.260
If you want to perform here,

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:44.750
your troupe will first have to become a recognized force in the acting world.

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:49.520
<i>A Midsummer Night's Dream</i>?

00:12:50.280 --> 00:12:51.260
Yup.

00:12:51.260 --> 00:12:53.360
I thought we could tackle Shakespeare this time.

00:12:54.050 --> 00:12:57.810
There's a young man in love with a beautiful woman called Hermia,

00:12:57.810 --> 00:13:00.940
but he's being pursued by another beautiful woman called Helena.

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:05.620
The four are accosted by lots of fairies when they get lost in a forest...

00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:09.810
and get caught up in conflict.Then, they become mixed up in unimaginable relationships...

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:13.430
caused by a mischievous little sprite called Puck.

00:13:13.990 --> 00:13:16.270
I'd like to make this play fun.

00:13:16.590 --> 00:13:21.640
Four young people falling in love and mischievous fairies.

00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:25.220
Rei, I want to be in this play.

00:13:25.890 --> 00:13:27.170
I have no objections.

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:28.780
Nor do I!

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:29.730
Should be no problem!

00:13:31.230 --> 00:13:34.220
Thank you all so much!

00:13:34.570 --> 00:13:36.550
You're fine acting in any role, aren't you?

00:13:36.550 --> 00:13:39.230
Yes! I'll give it my very best!

00:13:39.510 --> 00:13:42.480
Then, you can play the role of Puck the fairy.

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:45.790
Really? You want me to play Puck?

00:13:45.790 --> 00:13:49.450
Puck needs to be played by the most skilled actor. He's an important character.

00:13:50.110 --> 00:13:52.420
I'm Puck, a fairy...

00:13:52.420 --> 00:13:54.760
What about the set pieces for the forest scenes?

00:13:54.760 --> 00:13:57.030
The underground theater is too small.

00:13:57.030 --> 00:13:59.600
If only we could use the Athena Theater for this production.

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:02.290
Woodland fairies.

00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:03.970
Woodlands.

00:14:05.300 --> 00:14:06.950
We should perform on an outdoor stage.

00:14:07.690 --> 00:14:11.770
We have all these seats and lights and greenery!

00:14:11.770 --> 00:14:14.250
This clearing can be our stage!

00:14:14.510 --> 00:14:17.360
There's a train station and a shopping district close by too.

00:14:17.360 --> 00:14:21.270
I'm sure all kinds of people will come along if we hang up some posters to advertise the show!

00:14:21.270 --> 00:14:23.550
It has to be exciting or people will get up and leave without a second thought.

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:25.520
This will really test our mettle!

00:14:25.520 --> 00:14:30.390
Right! Let's pack this place out and show the Athena Theater what we're made of!

00:14:30.730 --> 00:14:31.970
Let's do it!

00:14:32.440 --> 00:14:35.710
So, you managed to rent an outdoor theater?

00:14:35.710 --> 00:14:37.220
And you've cast Maya as Puck?

00:14:37.550 --> 00:14:40.280
Please let her be in the show, ma'am.

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:42.690
We're all begging you to let her act in our show.

00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:45.050
"The lady has it right:

00:14:45.050 --> 00:14:48.060
I am the sprite that stalks the night!"

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:50.980
Puck is energetic and loves playing pranks.

00:14:50.980 --> 00:14:53.600
But my movements seem pretty dull.

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:57.100
I bet Ayumi's movements would be more graceful than this.

00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:00.190
Ms. Tsukikage!

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:04.170
He runs like the wind and bounds about like a flea.

00:15:04.660 --> 00:15:08.680
You think he's snuck in like a shadow when he disappears like light.

00:15:09.240 --> 00:15:14.240
It's very hard to play Puck if you can't control your body.

00:15:15.090 --> 00:15:18.980
Shall I teach you the foundation of Puck's movements?

00:15:19.570 --> 00:15:23.320
Get six people to form a circle and give balls to three of them.

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:25.680
Maya, you stand in the middle.

00:15:26.810 --> 00:15:32.810
Those balls will be thrown around the circle and you have to make sure you don't get hit by them.

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:34.930
Ma'am!

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:39.430
Puck's movements are based on his reflexes!

00:15:40.760 --> 00:15:42.460
His reflexes?

00:15:42.720 --> 00:15:45.100
This is good. Turn that on, will you?

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:51.190
Is the music part of the exercise?

00:15:51.190 --> 00:15:52.890
You'll see.

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:57.720
She's about to learn the kind of acting that can't be learned with the heart.

00:15:58.770 --> 00:15:59.770
Go!

00:16:05.850 --> 00:16:08.030
She can't stop even for a moment!

00:16:17.900 --> 00:16:19.050
Stop!

00:16:19.820 --> 00:16:23.640
I want you to do this exercise for an hour every day until the opening show.

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:27.790
If you had been the real Puck, you would have avoided every single one of those balls.

00:16:31.450 --> 00:16:33.000
They're doing that exercise again today.

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:33.780
But what are they doing exactly?

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:37.610
It's already been a week.

00:16:37.610 --> 00:16:39.780
Sayaka, haven't you noticed?

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:43.330
I guess now that you mention it, she seems to have picked up the rhythm.

00:16:44.070 --> 00:16:47.590
It's like her body has unconsciously remembered it.

00:16:47.910 --> 00:16:50.270
Movements based on rhythm are considered beautiful.

00:16:50.270 --> 00:16:52.550
So, that's what this is about.

00:16:52.750 --> 00:16:54.380
"About the wind go swifter than the wind,

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:56.840
And Helena of Athens look thou find."

00:16:57.170 --> 00:16:58.840
"I go, I go,

00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:03.280
look how I go, swifter than arrow from the Tartar's bow."

00:17:02.210 --> 00:17:03.270
Again!

00:17:03.640 --> 00:17:04.350
Yes, ma'am!

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:07.610
"Swifter than arrow from the Tartar's bow."

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:09.600
"Look how I go..."

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:12.190
What does he mean by those words?

00:17:12.190 --> 00:17:14.930
They mean I'm supposed to be very agile.

00:17:15.210 --> 00:17:18.090
So, how should Puck move when he's saying that?

00:17:18.090 --> 00:17:20.760
He's moving as if to say "Look at me!"

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:22.520
Do it again!

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:23.280
Yes, ma'am!

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:29.220
"Swifter than arrow from the Tartar's bow."

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:44.270
"I go,

00:17:45.390 --> 00:17:50.000
look how I go, swifter than arrow from the Tartar's bow."

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:52.460
I dodged it.

00:17:52.810 --> 00:17:55.390
I did it without thinking, sensing the ball coming at me from behind my head.

00:17:55.650 --> 00:17:57.850
Reflexes! This is how Puck moves!

00:17:58.370 --> 00:18:00.900
Ma'am, please let me try again!

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:03.190
"I go, I go,

00:18:03.190 --> 00:18:05.170
look how I go,

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:09.930
swifter than arrow from the Tartar's bow."

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:15.130
I want you to remember this action.

00:18:15.790 --> 00:18:19.310
Please, teach me more, ma'am!

00:18:19.310 --> 00:18:21.620
I know I can do even better!

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:24.400
I can grasp Puck's movements... his character!

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:26.920
The exercise with the balls is enough.

00:18:27.360 --> 00:18:31.130
Your body should already know what it should be doing.

00:18:31.560 --> 00:18:34.310
I still can't dodge all of them though...

00:18:34.310 --> 00:18:37.090
and you said that if I were Puck, I'd be able to dodge them all!

00:18:42.090 --> 00:18:45.920
I want you to disguise yourself as Puck using these things.

00:18:53.280 --> 00:18:54.940
Very well.

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:56.100
And how do you feel now?

00:18:57.150 --> 00:19:00.140
Like I've really become him.

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:02.630
Then, I want you to dodge the balls as Puck.

00:19:03.520 --> 00:19:05.130
As Puck?

00:19:06.050 --> 00:19:07.400
As Puck.

00:19:07.800 --> 00:19:08.750
What should I do?

00:19:09.760 --> 00:19:11.010
I am...

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:16.490
Puck.

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:18.810
Begin!

00:19:23.810 --> 00:19:24.850
She's...

00:19:40.460 --> 00:19:41.690
It's Puck!

00:19:41.690 --> 00:19:42.720
She's become Puck!

00:19:42.750 --> 00:19:56.290
Fire Extinguisher

00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:44.880
Maya...

00:19:45.670 --> 00:19:50.450
You need to unearth the treasure within you quickly!

00:19:50.890 --> 00:19:55.920
Oh... if only we had more time!

00:19:56.790 --> 00:19:59.090
You said Tsukikage and Ikkakujuu?

00:19:59.090 --> 00:20:01.310
Yes. Have you heard of them?

00:20:01.310 --> 00:20:05.090
<i>Heard of them?</i> You've made some formidable enemies, Mr. Director!

00:20:05.390 --> 00:20:10.420
When they first opened their theater, the neighboring Orion Theater became a ghost town!

00:20:18.600 --> 00:20:20.060
You need to move forward!

00:20:20.060 --> 00:20:23.180
This is an interesting concept, putting on a show outside.

00:20:23.630 --> 00:20:27.660
There's no real overheads and passersby will definitely be intrigued...

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:29.370
and may even stop to watch the performance.

00:20:30.180 --> 00:20:31.620
What are you talking about?

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:34.170
You're absolutely right.

00:20:34.510 --> 00:20:39.800
And yet, theatergoers who buy tickets at expensive theaters won't leave their seats...

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:42.740
once the show has started, unless the show is absolutely horrendous.

00:20:42.740 --> 00:20:44.450
But this is different.

00:20:44.450 --> 00:20:47.030
If our show's no good, our audience can just get up and leave at any point.

00:20:47.030 --> 00:20:52.620
That's why we believe this will be the best proof of our skill if we put on a successful show here.

00:20:52.620 --> 00:20:54.500
The gall of you!

00:20:55.010 --> 00:20:56.860
Okay, put on your show!

00:20:56.860 --> 00:21:00.160
If you can draw a crowd larger than what we get at the Athena theater,

00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:03.010
I'll admit your troupe has skill.

00:21:03.680 --> 00:21:07.820
So, are you saying, if we can do that,

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:10.100
you'll let us perform at the Athena Theater?

00:21:10.880 --> 00:21:12.500
I will consider it, yes.

00:21:12.820 --> 00:21:14.280
You mean it?

00:21:14.280 --> 00:21:15.630
Then, I...

00:21:16.590 --> 00:21:19.040
shall act as a witness to your promise.

00:21:19.860 --> 00:21:21.860
Masumi Hayami!

00:21:22.390 --> 00:21:24.890
Is there a problem with me standing witness to this promise?

00:21:24.890 --> 00:21:27.400
Of course not!

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:29.710
Okay then.

00:21:29.710 --> 00:21:31.370
If, during your three-day stint,

00:21:31.370 --> 00:21:34.960
you have even one more person in your audience than we do,

00:21:34.960 --> 00:21:36.980
I'll let you perform your show at the Athena Theater.

00:21:42.460 --> 00:21:44.300
We did it, Maya!

00:22:03.940 --> 00:22:18.080
Chikazukitai noni toozaketeshimau

00:22:03.940 --> 00:22:18.080
I want to be close to you, but you're distancing yourself.

00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:31.320
Dakishimetai toki wazato hanareteshimau

00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:31.320
When I want to hold you, you deliberately run away.

00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:44.070
Marude jishaku no N to N no you da ne

00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:44.070
We're like two poles on a magnet...

00:22:44.070 --> 00:22:55.190
Otagai amari nimo nisugita seikana?

00:22:44.070 --> 00:22:55.190
Maybe we're too alike?

00:22:55.190 --> 00:23:09.920
Motto motto sunao na hitomi de mitsureba

00:22:55.190 --> 00:23:09.920
If you allow your eyes to see the truth,

00:23:09.920 --> 00:23:21.510
Yodonderu izumi mo suki tooru hazusa

00:23:09.920 --> 00:23:21.510
even quagmires will become crystal clear.

00:23:21.850 --> 00:23:24.200
What are you plotting now?

00:23:24.870 --> 00:23:31.570
You think I'll believe that frigid workaholic just because he's giving "friendly" advice now?

00:23:32.510 --> 00:23:37.260
I won't give up on <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>, no matter what obstacles lie in my path.

00:23:38.020 --> 00:23:39.200
But...

00:23:39.580 --> 00:23:46.320
this show must succeed or else all of us will be back at square one!

00:23:45.790 --> 00:23:51.580
Episode 33 - The Miracle of the Outdoor Theater

00:23:46.810 --> 00:23:50.900
Please, I beg you! Don't leave your seats!
